Arena CEO @ml_angelopoulos on what frontier labs have to do to react to DeepSeek, Qwen, and Kimi pricing this aggressively:
"The thing that's most interesting about this is the price-performance trade-offs. The leaderboard shows you just the raw score, and it is true that Opus 5 Max, I believe it's even statistically significant, the difference between that and Kimi K3."
"When you look at the cost performance trade-offs, for the most expensive tasks, it's still Anthropic that's number one. But then you go down the list and it's Kimi, it's Qwen, it's GLM, it's DeepSeek. Look at that gap for DeepSeek. This is one of the largest bends in the Pareto frontier that we've ever seen."
"This speaks to Brent's question. You can barely see the costs on the plot. It's deprecated so many models. Like this model used to be the Pareto frontier, DeepSeek V4 Flash High Preview, deprecated. Not relevant anymore. MiMo V2.5, not relevant anymore. Hy3, not relevant anymore."
